--- !u!114 &1559293224
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1559293222}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 45e279c791392b44394b9e7dbe2b18f6, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  jokeButton: {fileID: 424653226}
  textBox: {fileID: 136915220}
  jokeText: {fileID: 122459745}
  dadJokes:
  - What do you call a woman with one leg? Eileen
  - Cargo space? No. Cargo road
  - I, for one, like roman numerals
  - I spotted an albino dalmatian once.  it was the least I could do
  - What do you call a werewolf youtuber? A lycansubscribe
  - I was going to tell y'all a joke about time travel, but you didn't like it.
  - What did batman order at the bar?  Just ice
  - You hear about this new restaurant karma?  They have no menu, you get what you
    deserve
  - What do you call a weaponized fish?  A pike
  - I threw my neighbor into a nuclear reactor and now he's dead. What should I do?! 
    Barium
  - What happens when someone slaps you at a high frequency?  It hertz
  - "I know 25 letters of alphabet   I don\u2019t know y"
  - Why did the Mexican throw his wife off the bridge?  Tequila!
  - I asked the farmer why he was having a headache  He replied "My grains"
  - Saw someone stopping on a bun the other day. He was on a roll
  - At what point does a joke become a dad joke? When it becomes apparent
  - Who is Jack and why does he have a singular mento?
  - What do you call a flower that runs on electricity? A power plant.
  - I have a coffee bean that sits next to me at work. We don't get a lot of work
    done; he talks a latte.
  - "Why do divers fall backward out of boats?\nBecause if they fell forward, they\u2019d
    still be in the boat."
  - 'Why do seagulls fly near the Sea?

    Because if they flew near the bay, they
    would be bagels.'
  - 'What''s the difference between a hot sweet potato and a pig thrown out the window?

    One
    is a heated yam and the other is a yeeted ham. '
  - 'What does the ocean say when looking at a bowl of salt?

    I sea salt'
  - 'What does the bi-lingual cat say?

    Woof'
  - 'Why did the kid throw a stick of butter out the window?

    To see a butter-fly'
  - 'What do you call a guy who never farts in public?

    A private tutor'
  - 'What kind of tree fits in your hand?

    A palm tree'
  - 'Did you hear? I invented a new word!

    "plagiarism"'
  - "Why did the chicken go to the s\xE9ance?\nTo get to the other side."
  - 'Why do sharks live in salt water?

    Pepper water makes them sneeze.'
  - "I\u2019m terrified of elevators\u2026 I\u2019ve been taking steps to avoid them."
  - "Why do they call them lifts in the UK & elevators in the US?\nBecause we\u2019re
    raised differently."
  - 'Elevator puns really push my buttons.

    They let me down.


    They are
    bad on so many levels.'
  - "What\u2019s the difference between a diameter and a radius?\nA radius."
  - "Why does a circle have 360\xB0?\nIt spent way too much time at university."
  - 'Did you hear about the mathematician who''s afraid of negative numbers?

    He''ll
    stop at nothing to avoid them.'
  - 'Why can''t you hear Pterry the pterodactyl going to the bathroom?

    His "p"
    is silent.'
  - "Two parrots are sitting on a perch.\nOne says to the other, \u201Cdo you smell
    fish?\u201D"
  - Why do Norwegian ships have barcodes on them? So when they come in to port, they
    can... Scandinavian
  - One day I was washing the car with my son, he turned to me and said "Dad why
    can't you just use a sponge instead?"
